@startuml
title Generic Information Model — Overview

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "Reality" {
  class "REALITY" as Reality
}

package "Semantic Core" {
  class Thing
  class Assertion
  class Configuration
  class Transition
  class Context
}

package "Reasoning & Interpretation" {
  class Observation
  class Projection
  class Identity
  class Intention
  class Opportunity
  class Constraint
  class Decision
}

package "Operations" {
  class Analysis
  class Synthesis
  class Evaluation
  class Selection
  class Mission
}

Reality --> Assertion : observed / reported
Assertion --> Configuration : forms / informs
Context --> Assertion : gives meaning
Context --> Configuration : scopes

Configuration --> Transition : may change through
Transition --> Configuration : produces / approaches

Observation ..> Assertion : evidence about
Projection ..> Configuration : possible future
Projection ..> Transition : possible consequence

Identity ..> Configuration : interpretation
Intention ..> Configuration : desired
Intention ..> Thing : held by

Opportunity ..> Assertion : enabling interpretation
Opportunity ..> Transition : enables

Constraint ..> Assertion : limiting interpretation
Constraint ..> Transition : constrains

Decision ..> Transition : selects / commits
Decision ..> Configuration : selects

Analysis ..> Assertion : decomposes
Analysis ..> Configuration : analyses

Synthesis ..> Assertion : combines
Synthesis ..> Configuration : proposes
Synthesis ..> Transition : proposes

Evaluation ..> Projection : compares
Evaluation ..> Transition : evaluates

Selection ..> Transition : selects

Mission ..> Transition : induces / tests

note right of Assertion
  Information about reality.

  May be:
  observed
  reported
  inferred
  intended
  projected

  Provenance, time and context
  distinguish these meanings.
end note

note right of Configuration
  A coherent, referable view
  of relevant information
  understood as a state or
  arrangement.

  Not necessarily a database
  entity with fixed fields.
end note

note right of Transition
  Meaningful change involving
  one or more Configurations.

  May be possible, selected,
  planned or performed.
end note

note bottom of Projection
  "What might happen?"

  Includes continuation:
  what may happen if prevailing
  dynamics continue.

  Therefore "do nothing" is not
  a special action.
end note

note bottom of Identity
  Higher-level concepts such as
  Identity, Vision, Goal,
  Opportunity and Obstacle are
  interpretations or views over
  the semantic core rather than
  mandatory primitive types.
end note

@enduml
